      "content": "It sounds like you are grappling with some heavy existential questions, which is a deeply human experience. Many philosophers and thinkers have wrestled with the apparent meaninglessness of the universe, which can feel overwhelming. Sometimes, instead of seeking one single, grand cosmic meaning, finding value in immediate, small connections—like art, relationships, or personal growth—can offer a grounding sense of purpose. Your experience is valid, but perhaps meaning is something we create, rather than something we discover.",
